 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Automatic Size and Variance Determination for Surface Splatting](7363-automatic-size-and-variance-determination-for-surface-splatt.md)
-This method improves visual quality by automatically computing radius and variance per splat based on local point density. It builds on this method by providing specific automatic formulas that prevent discontinuities and artifacts associated with improper parameter choices.
+This method improves the visual quality of surface splatting on close-up views by automatically computing the radius ($r_i$) and variance ($v_i$) for each splat to ensure hole-free rendering and smooth blending, comparable to polygon rendering. Unlike methods that use global or fixed local variance and size, this approach calculates these parameters per-splat based on local point density, balancing blurriness and aliasing without manual user adjustment. It builds on [Splat Radius Adjustment Based on Normal Angle](1264-splat-radius-adjustment-based-on-normal-angle.md) by providing the specific automatic formulas for size and variance that prevent the discontinuities and artifacts associated with improper parameter choices.
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per splat for radius calculation, assuming normal vectors are pre-computed [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory per splat for storing the calculated radius [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Prevents holes in surface splatting when samples are elevated, adapting to local surface geometry [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Relies on heuristic constants (0.1, 0.9) which may not be optimal for all datasets [S1, unofficial]. Does not account for view-dependent foreshortening (unlike EWA Splatting) [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to Use:** Surface splatting of regularly sampled point clouds where elevation variance causes gaps [S1, unofficial].
-- **When Not to Use:** When view-dependent distortion is significant (use EWA Splatting) or when automatic density-based sizing is preferred [S1, unofficial].
